-- title:
--   Artin–Rees for Hom modules
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and $I \subseteq B$ an ideal, and let $M$ and $N$ be $B$-modules that are module-finite over $B$ (i.e. finitely generated). The assertion is the existence of a natural number $c$, depending only on $B$, $I$, $M$ and $N$, such that for every natural number $n$ and every $B$-linear map $g : M \to N$, if the range of $g$ is contained in the submodule $I^{n+c} \cdot \top$ of $N$ — that is, in $I^{n+c}N$, the submodule generated by products of elements of $I^{n+c}$ with elements of $N$ — then $g$, viewed as an element of the $B$-module $M \to_{\text{lin}} N$ of $B$-linear maps, lies in the submodule $I^{n} \cdot \top$ of $M \to_{\text{lin}} N$, i.e. in $I^{n} \operatorname{Hom}_B(M,N)$. Note the order of quantifiers: a single shift $c$ works uniformly for all $n$ and all $g$ simultaneously.
--
--   This is the Artin–Rees lemma transported to $\operatorname{Hom}$: the filtration of $\operatorname{Hom}_B(M,N)$ by $\{g : g(M) \subseteq I^nN\}$ is cofinal with the filtration by $I^n\operatorname{Hom}_B(M,N)$ (the reverse inclusion being trivial). It is used as a purely algebraic input in the deformation-theoretic constructions with presheaves of $\mathcal{O}$-modules, where approximate cocycles and coboundaries must be corrected at a controlled loss of $I$-adic precision.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LinearMap_exists_forall_mem_pow_smul_top_of_range_le_pow_smul.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
